---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About Monarque" description="Learn about the Monarque Astro theme and its premium editorial design system.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[1180px] px-6 py-16 md:px-10 md:py-24">
    <h1 class="display max-w-4xl text-5xl leading-tight md:text-7xl">Monarque is built for premium editorial publishing.</h1>
    <div class="prose mt-10 max-w-3xl">
      <p>
        Monarque is a reusable Astro and Tailwind CSS theme for luxury magazines, curated blogs, independent journals, and brand publications that need fast pages, refined typography, and content that remains crawlable without client-side rendering.
      </p>
      <p>
        The theme favors static HTML, typed content collections, responsive Astro image handling, accessible landmarks, visible focus states, canonical metadata, RSS, robots, sitemap generation, and Open Graph defaults.
      </p>
      <p>
        Buyers can replace the demo posts, authors, categories, navigation, social links, and imagery from centralized files without chasing project-specific assumptions through the codebase.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
